{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"## Target\n`src/rebar/llm/plan_review/det_floor.py` — **793 LOC** on origin/main against the 800-LOC hard cap\n(7 lines of headroom).\n\n## The concern boundary: BLOCKING checks vs NEVER-BLOCKING checks\n\nThe module's own docstring already states the invariant this split cuts along: \"The only sound,\nunambiguous blockers are therefore **P1, P4 (description), P5 (cycle), P8, P10, and P11**.\nEverything else is advisory or coverage-only.\"\n\nThat documented boundary is also a real seam in the CALL GRAPH. The four never-blocking checks —\n**P2 resolution**, **P3 package-existence**, **P6 AC/DD quality**, **P7 destructive-sniff** — have\nZERO call edges, inbound or outbound, to any other function that stays in `det_floor.py`:\n\n- `p2_resolution` and `p3_package_existence` call only `rebar.grounding.refute_absence` (lazily\n  imported) plus their own private extraction regexes `_FILE_REF_RE` / `_PKG_REF_RE`.\n- `p6_ac_quality` is a pure aggregation hub over the ALREADY-EXTRACTED advisory-lint siblings:\n  `det_operator_attested.ac_item_lines`, `det_clarity.vague_hits_in_line`,\n  `det_lint._verify_command_strings` / `_lint_verify_command`,\n  `det_operator_attested.operator_evidence_issues`,\n  `det_measurement_provenance.provenance_issues`, `det_citation.unbacked_citations`. Moving it puts\n  the hub in a module beside its spokes instead of in the floor's core.\n- `p7_destructive` calls nothing; it owns `_DESTRUCTIVE_RE` / `_SAFEGUARD_RE` outright.\n\nThe checks that STAY are the ones that are actually connected: `p1_readiness_shape` and\n`p4_oversize` both call `_count_ac_items`; `p1_readiness_shape` calls `_clarity_score`; `p4_oversize`\ncalls `_description_limit`; `p8_reviewability` calls `est_tokens`; `p5_task_dag` calls\n`det_lint._find_cycle` / `_file_interference`. Cutting between those two sets removes 246 lines\nwithout severing a single existing call edge.\n\n## Established precedent this follows\n`det_clarity.py` (P10/P11) and `det_lint.py` (P9 + pure helpers) were extracted from this same\nmodule on this same seam and re-exported from `det_floor.py`. This change is the third application\nof a pattern the package already uses, including its cycle-avoidance contract:\n`from __future__ import annotations` + `TYPE_CHECKING` for the `DetResult` / `PlanContext`\nannotations and a lazy `from .det_floor import DetResult` inside each function body, so there is no\nruntime import back into `det_floor`.\n\n## What moves\nNew module `src/rebar/llm/plan_review/det_advisory.py` receives, byte-for-byte:\n`_FILE_REF_RE`, `p2_resolution`, `_PKG_REF_RE`, `p3_package_existence`, `p6_ac_quality`,\n`_DESTRUCTIVE_RE`, `_SAFEGUARD_RE`, `p7_destructive`.\n\n`det_floor.py` remains the ENTRY MODULE and dispatcher: it keeps `DetResult`, `PlanContext`,\n`est_tokens`, the `DET_CHECKS` tuple, `run_det_floor`, and the finding/coverage aggregation\n(`det_finding_has_subject`, `det_blocking_findings`, `det_advisory_findings`, `det_coverage`), and\nre-exports all four moved checks so every existing import point and every `det_floor.<check>`\nattribute access keeps resolving unchanged.\n\n## Why the retained half is the half that stays\nThree tests bind to the `det_floor` MODULE OBJECT and would silently stop testing anything if their\ntarget moved:\n- `tests/unit/test_plan_review.py` monkeypatches `det_floor.DET_CHECKS`.\n- `tests/unit/test_af77_config_fault.py` monkeypatches `det_floor.run_det_floor`.\n- `tests/unit/test_plan_review_prerequisites.py`, `..._heldout.py` monkeypatch\n  `sizing.det_floor.est_tokens`.\n\nAll three targets are in the RETAINED half. `_clarity_score`, `_count_ac_items` and\n`_description_limit` are imported by name from `det_floor` by lockstep/migration tests and also\nstay. No moved symbol is monkeypatched anywhere; every reference to a moved symbol is either a call\nthrough the re-export or a `from ... det_floor import` that the re-export satisfies.\n\n## Sizes\n`det_floor.py` 793 -> ~550 (approx 250 lines / 31% headroom); `det_advisory.py` ~300. Both inside the\n200-500 target band; neither under 100.\n\n## Registry sweep (path-keyed artifacts)\nChecked before implementing, updated in the same change if they fire:\n- `.github/complexity-baseline.json` — grep confirms **zero** entries keyed to\n  `src/rebar/llm/plan_review/det_floor.py`, so no moved symbol carries a ceiling and the ratchet\n  cannot report `new>0`. Re-verified with `scripts/check_complexity_baseline.py --check`.\n- `tests/scripts/test_llm_seam_clean_heldout.py` `_OWNED_FILES` / `_MARKER_BUDGET` — lists\n  `llm/plan_review/det_floor.py`. No config read moves (`_description_limit`, the module's only\n  `compose_config` call, stays), so the new module must report zero config-ownership findings and\n  zero `# read-via:` markers; verified by running `scripts/check_config_ownership.py`.\n- `.github/module-size-limit.txt` — NOT touched. The gate and `tests/module_size_support.py` are\n  path-agnostic (`rglob`), so the new file needs no registration.\n- `docs/plan-review-gate.md` and `src/rebar/llm/plan_review/registry.py` name `det_floor.py` as the\n  layer-1 home; docstring/prose repointed to name the new sibling. Prose only, no assertions.\n\n## Verification\n- `pytest tests/unit/test_plan_review.py tests/unit/test_det_floor_clarity.py\n  tests/unit/test_det_floor_operator_attested.py tests/unit/test_g5_decomp_det.py\n  tests/unit/test_plan_review_prerequisites.py tests/unit/test_af77_config_fault.py\n  tests/unit/test_ticket_description_limit.py tests/unit/test_a8e5_det_hygiene_edge.py\n  tests/unit/test_module_size_contract.py tests/scripts/test_llm_seam_clean_heldout.py\n  tests/interfaces/lifecycle/test_criteria_heading_collapse.py` — all pass with NO test file edited\n  to accommodate the move.\n- `make lint`, `make typecheck`, `python scripts/check_complexity_baseline.py --check`.\n- `wc -l` on both files.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] `wc -l src/rebar/llm/plan_review/det_floor.py` reports at most 720 lines, and\n      `wc -l src/rebar/llm/plan_review/det_advisory.py` reports at least 100 lines.\n- [ ] `det_advisory.py` contains `p2_resolution`, `p3_package_existence`, `p6_ac_quality` and\n      `p7_destructive`, and `det_floor.py` re-exports all four so\n      `from rebar.llm.plan_review.det_floor import p6_ac_quality` still resolves.\n- [ ] `git diff --stat origin/main -- tests/` shows no test file changed except a prose-only\n      docstring repoint, and the listed pytest selection passes.\n- [ ] `git diff origin/main -- .github/module-size-limit.txt` is empty.\n- [ ] `make lint` and `make typecheck` exit 0 and\n      `python scripts/check_complexity_baseline.py --check` reports `new=0 increased=0`.\n- [ ] The commit message names the blocking-vs-never-blocking concern boundary and states the\n      call-graph evidence for it.\n"}},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1787186926996180001,"uuid":"39396c05-868a-4b4a-8f78-9acdcf9285a3"}